module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.RelativeProjGluing
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.RelativeProjSectionRings
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared.MapDomain
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.QuasicoherentBaseChange

/-!
# The affine charts of a relative projective spectrum

Let `s` be a relative `Proj` situation: a scheme `s.base` carrying a quasi-coherent,
commutative, nonnegatively graded algebra over its structure sheaf. Over an affine open `U` of
the base, the graded ring of local sections `s.sectionRing U` has a projective spectrum
`Proj (s.sectionRingGrading U)`, and this file builds the two morphisms that make those spectra
into charts of a scheme over the base:

* the structure morphism `Proj (s.sectionRingGrading U) ⟶ U`, obtained from the canonical map
  `Γ(S, U) → s.sectionRing U` and the affine identification of `U`;
* for `U ≤ V` affine opens, the comparison morphism
  `Proj (s.sectionRingGrading U) ⟶ Proj (s.sectionRingGrading V)` induced by restriction of
  homogeneous sections.

The comparison morphism exists because restriction is *everywhere defined* on the projective
spectrum, and that is the one piece of real geometry here: quasi-coherence of the homogeneous
pieces makes `𝒜ₙ(U)` the base change of `𝒜ₙ(V)` along `Γ(S, V) → Γ(S, U)`, so every
positive-degree homogeneous section over `U` is a `Γ(S, U)`-combination of restrictions of
positive-degree homogeneous sections over `V`, and the irrelevant ideal of `s.sectionRing U` is
contained in the ideal generated by the image of the irrelevant ideal of `s.sectionRing V`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.gradedSectionRestriction` is restriction of homogeneous local
  sections, as a homomorphism of graded rings.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.sectionRingZeroMap` identifies `Γ(S, U)` with the degree-zero
  part of the section ring over `U`.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.projInclusionToOpen` is the structure morphism of the chart
  over `U`.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.projInclusionMap` is the comparison morphism of charts.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.localData` assembles the charts of a situation into the local
  gluing datum `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data`, given the two topological properties of the
  comparison morphism that `Charts/Descent.lean` proves.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.mem_span_range_restrict`: the sections of a
  quasi-coherent module over an affine open are spanned by the restrictions of its sections over
  a larger affine open.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.gradedSectionRestriction_of` and
  `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.gradedSectionRestriction_baseMap`: the graded restriction map on
  a homogeneous section, and its compatibility with the maps from the structure sheaf.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.sectionRingBaseMap_mul_of`: multiplying a homogeneous section
  by the image of a function on the base is the module action of that function.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.irrelevant_le_map_gradedSectionRestriction`: the irrelevant
  ideal over `U` is generated by the restrictions of the irrelevant ideal over `V`.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.projInclusionDomain_eq_top`: the comparison morphism of
  projective spectra is defined on all of `Proj (s.sectionRingGrading U)`.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.gradedSectionRestriction_id`,
  `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.gradedSectionRestriction_comp` and
  `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.sectionRingZeroMap_restrict`: restriction of graded sections is
  functorial and compatible with the degree-zero identifications.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.projInclusion_isPullback_of`: the chart square is cartesian,
  granted those two topological properties.

## Implementation notes

`projInclusionMap` is `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` of the graded restriction homomorphism, which
Mathlib provides exactly under the hypothesis
`irrelevant_le_map_gradedSectionRestriction` proved here. The weaker statement
`projInclusionDomain_eq_top`, phrased with the open domain
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared.mapDomain` of a graded ring homomorphism, is deduced from
it; it is the form in which Tag 01NO states that the morphism is everywhere defined, and it is
strictly weaker, since `mapDomain` is all of the spectrum as soon as the irrelevant ideal is
contained in the *radical* of the image.

The chart structure morphism agrees with `Stacks.RelativeProj.chartToOpen` of the family of
graded rings indexed by the affine opens of the base
(`projInclusionToOpen_eq`), and the comparison morphism agrees with
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Data.map` of the datum assembled in `localData`. Those two agreements are
what let the gluing of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/RelativeProjGluing.lean` be used for a situation without
any further comparison of definitions.

`localData` takes as hypotheses the two topological properties of the comparison morphism — that
it is an open immersion, and that its image is the preimage of `U` in the chart over `V` — and
turns them into the local gluing datum. Together they are the cartesianness half of Tag 01NO; by
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.isPullback` they are equivalent to it, given the commuting
square, which `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data.commSq` supplies from `sectionRingZeroMap_restrict`. Both
are proved in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProj/Charts/Descent.lean`, which discharges
them and attaches the `@[stacks 01NO "the cartesian square"]` attribute; nothing in this file may
be read as a proof of that clause.

The membership transport `memOfEq` is a private helper. It exists because
`Scheme.ringCatSheaf` is a structure copy of a `CategoryTheory.Sheaf`, so a `rewrite` whose
motive mentions a section module over it fails its type check at `implicit` transparency; doing
the substitution on a bare element of the section ring keeps the motive away from those
projections.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite DirectSum
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange

/-- **The sections of a quasi-coherent module over an affine open are spanned by restrictions.**
For affine opens `U ≤ V` of a scheme and `M` quasi-coherent, every section of `M` over `U` is a
`Γ(X, U)`-linear combination of restrictions of sections of `M` over `V`. This is the surjective
half of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.isBaseChange_restrictₗ`. -/
public theorem mem_span_range_restrict {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent]
    {U V : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (h : U ≤ V) (a : Γ(M, U)) :
    a ∈ Submodule.span Γ(X, U)
      (Set.range fun b : Γ(M, V) => (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op) b) := by
  let := algebraOfLE X h
  let := moduleOfLE M h
  let := isScalarTowerOfLE M h
  have hbc := isBaseChange_restrictₗ M hU hV h
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hbc.equiv.surjective a
  induction z using TensorProduct.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | tmul r b =>
      rw [hbc.equiv_tmul]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨b, rfl⟩)
  | add z w hz hw => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ hz hw

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange

namespace Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation

variable (s : Situation.{u}) (U V : s.base.Opens) (h : U ≤ V)

/-- Restriction of the graded ring of homogeneous local sections along an inclusion of opens. -/
public noncomputable def gradedSectionRestriction :
    s.sectionRingGrading V →+*ᵍ s.sectionRingGrading U where
  toRingHom := s.sectionRingRestrict U V h
  map_mem := by
    intro n x hx
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact ⟨_, ((sectionRingStructure s).restrict_of U V h n a).symm⟩

/-- On a homogeneous section, the graded restriction map is restriction in that homogeneous
piece. -/
public theorem gradedSectionRestriction_of (n : ℕ) (a : s.sectionPieces V n) :
    gradedSectionRestriction s U V h (DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces V) n a) =
      DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n
        ((s.algebra.piece (n : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op a) :=
  (sectionRingStructure s).restrict_of U V h n a

/-- The graded restriction map is compatible with the maps from the structure sheaf. -/
public theorem gradedSectionRestriction_baseMap (r : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) :
    gradedSectionRestriction s U V h (s.sectionRingBaseMap V r) =
      s.sectionRingBaseMap U (s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.map (homOfLE h).op r) :=
  (sectionRingStructure s).restrict_baseMap U V h r

/-- Multiplying a homogeneous section by the image of a function on the base is the module
action of that function on that homogeneous piece. -/
public theorem sectionRingBaseMap_mul_of (n : ℕ)
    (r : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U)) (a : s.sectionPieces U n) :
    s.sectionRingBaseMap U r * DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n a =
      DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n (r • a) := by
  have key : ∀ (d : ℤ) (_ : d = (n : ℤ)) (x : (s.algebra.piece d).val.obj (op U)),
      x ≍ a → (r • x) ≍ (r • a) := by
    intro d hd x hx
    subst hd
    rw [eq_of_heq hx]
  rw [sectionRingBaseMap, (sectionRingStructure s).baseMap_apply, DirectSum.of_mul_of]
  refine DirectSum.of_eq_of_gradedMonoid_eq (Sigma.ext (zero_add n) ?_)
  refine ((sectionRingStructure s).mul_homogeneous U 0 n _ a).trans ?_
  have h2 := (s.algebra.mul ((0 : ℕ) : ℤ) (n : ℤ)).map_smul_left (op U) r
    (s.algebra.one.eval (op U)) a
  rw [h2]
  exact key _ (by simp) _ (s.algebra.one_mul (n : ℤ) (op U) a)

/-- The image of a function on the base is homogeneous of degree zero. -/
public theorem sectionRingBaseMap_mem_zero (r : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U)) :
    s.sectionRingBaseMap U r ∈ s.sectionRingGrading U 0 :=
  ⟨_, ((sectionRingStructure s).baseMap_apply U r).symm⟩

/-- Transport of ideal membership along an equation of sections. Stated separately because the
substitution then happens in a type with no dependence on the open, which keeps the motive away
from the projections of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ringCatSheaf`. -/
private theorem memOfEq {R : Type*} [Semiring R] {I : Ideal R} {y z : R} (hyz : y = z)
    (hy : y ∈ I) : z ∈ I := hyz ▸ hy

/-- Every positive-degree homogeneous section over `U` lies in the ideal generated by the
restrictions of the positive-degree homogeneous sections over `V`. This is the element-level
form of `irrelevant_le_map_gradedSectionRestriction`, and the place where quasi-coherence of the
homogeneous pieces is used. -/
private theorem projIrrSpan (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) :
    ∀ d : ℕ, 0 < d → ∀ g ∈ s.sectionRingGrading U d,
      g ∈ Ideal.span ((gradedSectionRestriction s U V h) ''
        ⋃ n > 0, (s.sectionRingGrading V n : Set (s.sectionRing V))) := by
  intro d hd g hg
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hg
  set ψ := gradedSectionRestriction s U V h
  set T : Set (s.sectionRing U) :=
    ψ '' ⋃ n > 0, (s.sectionRingGrading V n : Set (s.sectionRing V))
  have hmem : ∀ b : s.sectionPieces V d,
      DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) d
        ((s.algebra.piece (d : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op b) ∈ Ideal.span T := by
    intro b
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces V) d b,
      Set.mem_biUnion hd ⟨b, rfl⟩, gradedSectionRestriction_of s U V h d b⟩
  have hspan : a ∈ Submodule.span (s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))
      (Set.range fun b : s.sectionPieces V d =>
        ((s.algebra.piece (d : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op) b) :=
    mem_span_range_restrict (s.algebra.piece (d : ℤ)) hU hV h a
  induction hspan using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx => obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hx; exact hmem b
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact Ideal.zero_mem _
  | add x y _ _ ihx ihy => rw [map_add]; exact Ideal.add_mem _ ihx ihy
  | smul r x _ ih =>
      exact memOfEq (sectionRingBaseMap_mul_of s U d r x) (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ ih)

/-- **The irrelevant ideal over `U` is generated by the restrictions of the irrelevant ideal
over `V`.** This is Mathlib's hypothesis for `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map`, so it is what makes
the comparison morphism of projective spectra exist. -/
public theorem irrelevant_le_map_gradedSectionRestriction (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) :
    HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (s.sectionRingGrading U) ≤
      (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (s.sectionRingGrading V)).map
        (gradedSectionRestriction s U V h) :=
  irrelevant_le_map_of_mem_span _ _ _ (projIrrSpan s U V h hU hV)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01NO.** The morphism of projective spectra induced by restriction of
homogeneous sections along an inclusion of affine opens is defined on all of
`Proj (s.sectionRingGrading U)`. -/
@[stacks 01NO "the everywhere-defined morphism"]
public theorem projInclusionDomain_eq_top (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) :
    mapDomain (s.sectionRingGrading V) (s.sectionRingGrading U)
      (gradedSectionRestriction s U V h) = ⊤ :=
  mapDomain_eq_top_of_irrelevant_le_map _ _ _
    (irrelevant_le_map_gradedSectionRestriction s U V h hU hV)

/-- The morphism of projective spectra induced by restriction of homogeneous sections. -/
public noncomputable def projInclusionMap (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) :
    Proj (s.sectionRingGrading U) ⟶ Proj (s.sectionRingGrading V) :=
  Proj.map (gradedSectionRestriction s U V h)
    (irrelevant_le_map_gradedSectionRestriction s U V h hU hV)

/-- The identification of the sections of the structure sheaf over `U` with the degree-zero part
of the graded ring of homogeneous local sections over `U`. -/
public noncomputable def sectionRingZeroMap :
    Γ(s.base, U) ⟶ CommRingCat.of (s.sectionRingGrading U 0) :=
  CommRingCat.ofHom ((GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (s.sectionRingGrading U)).comp
    (s.sectionRingBaseMap U))

/-- The structure morphism of the chart over an affine open `U`: the projective spectrum of the
graded ring of sections over `U`, as a scheme over `U`. -/
public noncomputable def projInclusionToOpen (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    Proj (s.sectionRingGrading U) ⟶ U.toScheme :=
  Proj.toSpecZero (s.sectionRingGrading U) ≫ Spec.map (sectionRingZeroMap s U) ≫ hU.isoSpec.inv

/-- The chart structure morphism of a situation is the chart structure morphism of the family of
graded section rings indexed by the affine opens of the base. -/
public theorem projInclusionToOpen_eq (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    projInclusionToOpen s U hU =
      chartToOpen (fun W : s.base.affineOpens => s.sectionRingGrading W.1) ⟨U, hU⟩
        (sectionRingZeroMap s U) := rfl

/-- Restricting homogeneous sections along the identity is the identity. -/
public theorem gradedSectionRestriction_id :
    gradedSectionRestriction s U U le_rfl = GradedRingHom.id (s.sectionRingGrading U) :=
  GradedRingHom.ext fun x =>
    congrArg (fun k : s.sectionRing U →+* s.sectionRing U => k x)
      ((sectionRingStructure s).restrict_id U)

/-- Restriction of homogeneous sections is functorial. -/
public theorem gradedSectionRestriction_comp (W : s.base.Opens) (hUV : U ≤ V) (hVW : V ≤ W) :
    gradedSectionRestriction s U W (hUV.trans hVW) =
      (gradedSectionRestriction s U V hUV).comp (gradedSectionRestriction s V W hVW) :=
  GradedRingHom.ext fun x =>
    congrArg (fun k : s.sectionRing W →+* s.sectionRing U => k x)
      ((sectionRingStructure s).restrict_comp U V W hUV hVW)

/-- Restriction of homogeneous sections is compatible with the degree-zero identifications. -/
public theorem sectionRingZeroMap_restrict :
    s.base.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op ≫ sectionRingZeroMap s U =
      sectionRingZeroMap s V ≫
        CommRingCat.ofHom (gradedSectionRestriction s U V h).gradedZeroRingHom := by
  ext r : 2
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  have h0 : ∀ (W : s.base.Opens) (x : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)),
      GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (s.sectionRingGrading W) (s.sectionRingBaseMap W x) =
        ⟨s.sectionRingBaseMap W x, sectionRingBaseMap_mem_zero s W x⟩ := fun W x =>
    GradedRing.projZeroRingHom'_apply_coe _ ⟨_, sectionRingBaseMap_mem_zero s W x⟩
  show ((GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (s.sectionRingGrading U)) (s.sectionRingBaseMap U
      (s.base.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op r)) : s.sectionRing U) =
    ((gradedSectionRestriction s U V h).gradedZeroRingHom
      ((GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (s.sectionRingGrading V)) (s.sectionRingBaseMap V r)) :
        s.sectionRing U)
  rw [h0 U (s.base.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op r), h0 V r]
  exact ((sectionRingStructure s).restrict_baseMap U V h r).symm

/-- The charts of a situation, as the local gluing datum of a relative projective spectrum.

The two hypotheses are the content of Tag 01NO that is not proved: that the comparison morphism
of charts is an open immersion, and that its image is the preimage of the smaller affine open.
Everything else a `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data` asks for is supplied by the results above. -/
public noncomputable def localData
    (hoi : ∀ {W W' : s.base.affineOpens} (hWW' : W ≤ W'),
      IsOpenImmersion (projInclusionMap s W.1 W'.1 hWW' W.2 W'.2))
    (hor : ∀ {W W' : s.base.affineOpens} (hWW' : W ≤ W'),
      projInclusionToOpen s W'.1 W'.2 ⁻¹ᵁ (s.base.homOfLE hWW').opensRange =
        (projInclusionMap s W.1 W'.1 hWW' W.2 W'.2).opensRange) :
    Data (fun W : s.base.affineOpens => s.sectionRingGrading W.1) where
  base W := sectionRingZeroMap s W.1
  restrict hWW' := gradedSectionRestriction s _ _ hWW'
  irrelevant_le {W W'} hWW' :=
    irrelevant_le_map_gradedSectionRestriction s W.1 W'.1 hWW' W.2 W'.2
  restrict_id W := gradedSectionRestriction_id s W.1
  restrict_comp hWW' hW'W'' := gradedSectionRestriction_comp s _ _ _ hWW' hW'W''
  base_restrict hWW' := sectionRingZeroMap_restrict s _ _ hWW'
  isOpenImmersion_map hWW' := hoi hWW'
  opensRange_map hWW' := hor hWW'

/-- The chart square of a situation is cartesian, granted the two topological properties of the
comparison morphism that are still open. This is the cartesian square of Tag 01NO; it carries no
`@[stacks]` attribute because its hypotheses are exactly the unproved part of that tag. -/
public theorem projInclusion_isPullback_of
    (hoi : ∀ {W W' : s.base.affineOpens} (hWW' : W ≤ W'),
      IsOpenImmersion (projInclusionMap s W.1 W'.1 hWW' W.2 W'.2))
    (hor : ∀ {W W' : s.base.affineOpens} (hWW' : W ≤ W'),
      projInclusionToOpen s W'.1 W'.2 ⁻¹ᵁ (s.base.homOfLE hWW').opensRange =
        (projInclusionMap s W.1 W'.1 hWW' W.2 W'.2).opensRange)
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) :
    CategoryTheory.IsPullback (projInclusionMap s U V h hU hV) (projInclusionToOpen s U hU)
      (projInclusionToOpen s V hV) (s.base.homOfLE h) :=
  (localData s hoi hor).isPullback (U := ⟨U, hU⟩) (V := ⟨V, hV⟩) h

end Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation

end
